From 1ea2b798c4c56d651d6a7ff12eca2ce8cd70f209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightMoss <lightmoss@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:43:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3326-r36sclone: run the CPU at the
 rates it reports

spruce's CPU modes on this board ask for 1416 MHz (Smart, Performance)
and 1512 MHz (Overclock), and cpufreq reports those rates, but the CPU
ran at 1248 or 1296 MHz: rockchip_adjust_power_scale() caps the APLL
and rockchip_get_pll_settings() programs the capped rate for any higher
request while reporting the requested one.

Two things set the cap. The 1.35 V rockchip,max-volt makes
rockchip_adjust_opp_by_irdrop() take the first OPP at 1.35 V as the
safe rate (1248 MHz on PVTM level L0, PLL scale 15), and
rockchip,bin-scaling-sel gives both speed bins PLL scale 13 (1296 MHz).

Raise rockchip,max-volt to 1.4 V, above every OPP here, so there is no
irdrop clamp, and opt in to rockchip,boot-max-freq (1296 MHz, as in
rk3326-oc.dtsi), with which LightMoss's boot.ini passes
max_cpufreq=1512 to make rockchip_adjust_power_scale() choose the PLL
scale for 1512 MHz. The 1416 and 1512 MHz OPPs get 1.35 V on every PVTM
level (L2 and L3 had 1.3/1.25 V): no OPP gets more than 1.35 V, the
voltage the CPU already runs 1248 and 1296 MHz at on L0/L1 chips. GPU
and DDR OPPs are unchanged.
---
 .../dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts   | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
index d44111ac1..dc0f092c1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
@@ -350,6 +350,33 @@ &cpu0_opp_table {
 	1               13
 	>;
 
+	/*
+	 * LightMoss: the CPU runs at the rates spruce's CPU modes ask for
+	 * (Smart and Performance up to 1416 MHz, Overclock 1512 MHz), not
+	 * below them. Otherwise the 1.35 V ceiling makes
+	 * rockchip_adjust_opp_by_irdrop() take 1248 MHz, the first OPP at it,
+	 * as the safe rate, and the bin scale above caps the PLL at 1296 MHz:
+	 * cpufreq reports the higher rates while rockchip_get_pll_settings()
+	 * programs the capped one. A ceiling above every OPP here leaves no
+	 * irdrop clamp, and boot.ini's max_cpufreq=1512 with
+	 * rockchip,boot-max-freq makes the kernel choose the PLL scale for
+	 * 1512 MHz (as arkos4clone's rk3326-oc.dtsi and ArkOS's boot.ini do).
+	 * No OPP is given more than 1.35 V, the voltage this CPU already runs
+	 * 1248 and 1296 MHz at; 1416 and 1512 MHz get it on every PVTM level.
+	 * (Rockchip's low-temperature adjustment still adds 50 mV below 0 C.)
+	 */
+	rockchip,max-volt = <1400000>;
+	rockchip,boot-max-freq = <1296000000>;
+
+	opp-1416000000 {
+		opp-microvolt-L2 = <1350000 1350000 1350000>;
+		opp-microvolt-L3 = <1350000 1350000 1350000>;
+	};
+
+	opp-1512000000 {
+		opp-microvolt-L2 = <1350000 1350000 1350000>;
+		opp-microvolt-L3 = <1350000 1350000 1350000>;
+	};
 };
 
 &display_subsystem {
